  "id": "15-vwap-excursion-response-20261006-web",
  "title": "VWAP excursion: return and first-touch response",
  "summary": "Fresh two-sigma departures show different return and response behavior by anchor and product. Complete-path denominators and shared-week uncertainty limit these to exploratory price evidence.",
  "publishedAt": "2026-10-06T23:09:36Z",
  "source": {
    "producer": "sahadeva",
    "runId": "20260929T234000Z_a15f"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "question",
      "title": "Question and scope",
      "body": "For ES, NQ and GC, what follows the first fresh two-sigma departure from each causal session VWAP, and what follows its first traded contact? The selected concise saved findings contain ten two-minute candles, a twenty-minute horizon, mirrored sides and four overlapping anchors. Longer-horizon evidence remains in the saved full tables."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "findings",
      "title": "Supported findings",
      "body": "Return probability depends strongly on the anchor population. Continuation-minus-fade endpoint differences are mixed, with several uncertain intervals. First-touch bounce endpoint rates can sit near one half while payoff distributions differ. No optimization or trading edge is inferred from selected rates."
    },
