    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "methods",
      "title": "Definitions and methods",
      "body": "Completed two-minute HLC3 is weighted by bar volume; population sigma is volume weighted. A first fresh strict close beyond two sigma is selected within a causal parent excursion. Entry is the next two-minute open. Primary touch is source one-minute range overlap with the tick-rounded ±one-tick evolving VWAP zone known at minute open; gap or reference overtake alone is not touch. Touch response begins after its containing two-minute candle closes. Upper departure continuation and upper-arrival bounce are long; lower counterparts are short. Continuation delta compares signed continuation with fade endpoint movement in native points. Bounce endpoint probability tests the signed terminal response, not a first-barrier winner or a trading win rate. Unavailable horizons are excluded from eligible outcome denominators. Saved marginal 95% intervals use shared ISO-week cluster draws."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "limitations",
      "title": "Limitations and uncertainty",
      "body": "Previously viewed, retrospectively complete history is exploratory: ES/NQ eligible dates begin in 2021 and GC in 2016, ending September 18, 2026. Anchors and thresholds are dependent. Bootstrap zero/all-success cells have unresolved boundary uncertainty, not certainty. Sparse support and exclusions remain in the saved coverage table. No order-flow delta, fills, costs, intraminute barrier order or realized profitability was tested. The optional Pine companion has not been independently compiled in its native environment."
    },
